From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shipwright <shipwright@invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:53:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the build warnings

Header enum helpers are inline instead of static, so each translation
unit no longer gets its own unused copy (-Wunused-function). Member
initialisers follow declaration order (-Wreorder). Unused variables
are removed, and a failed send() on the client socket is now logged
instead of ignored. Loop and size comparisons use size_t
(-Wsign-compare). In the vendored uSockets only, GCC 12+'s
-Wuse-after-free is turned off for a pointer comparison it misreads.
---
